From f66268702337264f5221c50d292139e71733ddbb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jason Perlow <jperlow@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 5 Aug 2026 18:25:42 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] Report RTFormat from vaQueryConfigAttributes for
 attribute-less configs

vaQueryConfigAttributes() is specified to return the attributes of a
configuration, but MediaDevice::QueryConfigAttributes() only echoes back
the attribute array that the caller happened to pass to vaCreateConfig().
MediaDevice::CreateConfig() stores that array verbatim and never records
the driver's own defaults, so a configuration created with
(attrib_list = NULL, num_attribs = 0) reports zero attributes and a client
has no way to discover which RT formats the configuration supports.

Chromium depends on exactly that sequence. VASupportedProfiles::
FillProfileInfo_Locked() deliberately creates a second, attribute-less
configuration -- "we don't pass required attributes here because we want
the driver to tell us all the supported RT formats" -- then scans the
result for VAConfigAttribRTFormat. With no attributes returned, none of
yuv420/yuv420_10/yuv422/yuv444 is ever set, is_any_profile_supported stays
false and the profile is rejected. The rejection is reported through
DLOG_IF(), which is compiled out of release builds, so every profile and
entrypoint fails silently: about:gpu lists no decoders at all while
ffmpeg and mpv work normally on the same driver, because they never call
vaQueryConfigAttributes().

Record the driver's own VAConfigAttribRTFormat in CreateConfig() when the
caller did not supply one. The value is obtained from the existing
GetConfigAttributes() dispatcher, so v4l2 and cme keep full control of
what they advertise and no per-codec knowledge is duplicated here.

Verified on a CIX Sky1 board (O6N, cix-vaapi 1.1.0 sources, Chrome 151):

  before: vaQueryConfigAttributes() returns num_attribs = 0 for all seven
          probed profile/entrypoint pairs; Chrome logs 15
          "FillProfileInfo_Locked failed" and about:gpu shows an empty
          "Video Acceleration Information" table.

  after:  num_attribs = 1 with RTFormat = VA_RT_FORMAT_YUV420, and
          VAProfileAV1Profile0 correctly reports
          VA_RT_FORMAT_YUV420|VA_RT_FORMAT_YUV420_10 via the existing
          IS_10BIT_PROFILE() path; Chrome logs no failures and about:gpu
          enumerates h264 baseline/main/high, vp9 profile0/profile2,
          hevc main/main10/still-picture and av1 main, each 144x144 to
          8192x8192.

No regression: ffmpeg -hwaccel vaapi decodes unchanged and
vaQuerySurfaceAttributes() still returns its full attribute set.

Signed-off-by: Jason Perlow <jperlow@gmail.com>
---
 devices/device_common.cpp | 25 +++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 25 insertions(+)

diff --git a/devices/device_common.cpp b/devices/device_common.cpp
index 34f837b..44f1928 100644
--- a/devices/device_common.cpp
+++ b/devices/device_common.cpp
@@ -175,6 +175,31 @@ VAStatus MediaDevice::CreateConfig(
             id, i, attrib_list[i].type, attrib_list[i].value);
     }
 
+    // vaQueryConfigAttributes() must report the config's *effective* attributes,
+    // not only those the caller happened to pass to vaCreateConfig(). Record the
+    // driver's own VAConfigAttribRTFormat when the caller did not specify one,
+    // otherwise a config created with (attrib_list = NULL, num_attribs = 0)
+    // reports zero attributes and clients cannot discover the supported RT
+    // formats. Chromium relies on exactly that: it creates an attribute-less
+    // config specifically so the driver will enumerate its RT formats, and
+    // rejects every profile when none come back.
+    bool has_rt_format = false;
+    for (const auto &attrib : config.attribs) {
+        if (attrib.type == VAConfigAttribRTFormat) {
+            has_rt_format = true;
+            break;
+        }
+    }
+    if (!has_rt_format) {
+        VAConfigAttrib rt_format;
+        rt_format.type = VAConfigAttribRTFormat;
+        rt_format.value = VA_ATTRIB_NOT_SUPPORTED;
+        if (GetConfigAttributes(profile, entrypoint, &rt_format, 1) == VA_STATUS_SUCCESS &&
+            rt_format.value != VA_ATTRIB_NOT_SUPPORTED) {
+            config.attribs.push_back(rt_format);
+        }
+    }
+
     CIX_VAAPI_INFO("Created config %d: profile %d, entrypoint %d\n", id, profile, entrypoint);
     *config_id = id;
     return VA_STATUS_SUCCESS;
